                <l xml:id="m-876e652d-807f-4233-aba6-d37d294664d0" facs="#m-2e7a3537-a1d3-48b7-aff1-8691dd0e72f0" label="text-like">THE FEAST OF PENTECOST.</l><l xml:id="m-cf12f6f9-e683-45f5-aca6-8d04fd315aaf" facs="#m-2619698b-3b85-432d-be12-f29c0b16afa4" label="text-like">WHIT SUNDAY.</l><l xml:id="m-c6e8c40d-cf91-4839-8354-bf77711ebcb3" facs="#m-3b045bc4-369d-4ef1-9f54-9c9c70df7d5e" label="text-like">AT FIRST VESPERS.</l><l xml:id="m-19aa6686-c05b-4636-90b6-c0257c41469b" facs="#m-b6a98618-f58a-4d55-af94-1d4230a26a7e" label="lyrics-like">All as at Second Vespers, p. 884, except the fifth Psalm, which is Laudáte</l><l xml:id="m-e64df3fb-c83c-4d5f-871f-ce5f81c7810f" facs="#m-0a88fa13-33e2-4c83-973f-c8541b676ea8" label="lyrics-like">Dóminum 7. c. 2. p. 168, and the followins:</l><l xml:id="m-66fc79ac-df36-4502-bf4d-a7bcf5cf96bb" facs="#m-b5521f17-afb9-43a1-8c2e-527b08704690" label="lyrics-like">V. Replé-ti sunt ómnes Spí-ri-tu Sáncto, alle-lú-ia.</l><l xml:id="m-b8550da5-dd18-44c0-8868-683a0c12da44" facs="#m-668683b4-3c65-406a-8080-c1ef056ccf7d" label="lyrics-like">N. Et coepérunt loqui, alle-lú-ia.</l><l xml:id="m-a393b743-3f72-442f-8bfa-b37f4e2da22b" facs="#m-c34d0cc1-e387-406c-b42d-2f84f267c3e7" label="text-like">At Magn.</l><l xml:id="m-0a17e56c-dbdd-4dab-824e-84d169818a67" facs="#m-0b2ae19a-dcb7-4cf6-a185-e69b2089ff7f" label="ambiguous">Ant. 1.D</l><l xml:id="m-0e591980-a2c2-41bc-a1c6-082b848df2e6" facs="#m-9db1bf59-f710-421d-b274-6e4b2af6057b" label="ambiguous">n</l><l xml:id="m-f04fd9eb-e162-4b08-bd34-f085742789a8" facs="#m-a64d950c-caa2-4843-bf56-46b257d2f9c3" label="lyrics-like">ON vos re-línquam* órphanos, alle-lú-ia : vá¬</l><l xml:id="m-c7a86555-74fa-4240-9063-214fc921540f" facs="#m-4e45d46f-ec94-4bd5-90f6-87eabf0927c5" label="lyrics-like">et gaudé-bit cor vé¬</l><l xml:id="m-544abbd0-13d1-4ffc-bf81-f03c92dce352" facs="#m-b09782ad-46d9-4ea7-8d69-656b3b1bcdd0" label="lyrics-like">do, et véni-o ad vos, alle-lú-ia:</l><l xml:id="m-2912906a-2898-4ab2-bcc1-ecc4c19cf0a1" facs="#m-e09cc1e2-51a6-4103-a34e-1faad897f826" label="lyrics-like">strum, alle-lú-ia. Eu o u a e.</l><l xml:id="m-730c5513-0ec7-4127-abf8-6a1542313b1a" facs="#m-4f102144-913f-463a-8306-1e09ce338db2" label="lyrics-like">cant. Magníficat. I. D. p. 207, or p. 213.</l><l xml:id="m-c1854359-1366-4f34-86e5-643861d4dc3c" facs="#m-aa894acd-0076-4eb7-bcf7-eca824b54b37" label="text-like">Tone of the Hymn at Compline.</l><l xml:id="m-9c81282b-1ab8-4635-b9ed-c150eda353e6" facs="#m-e69ea0ed-9ebf-45da-832a-21e5df0107e2" label="ambiguous">1.</l><l xml:id="m-27efd9b1-59cf-40e1-a64f-1ae8b9d823da" facs="#m-e74f96fa-eb9f-4c79-b5a8-d28386c2fbb7" label="lyrics-like">E lú-cis ante términum, Ré-rum Cre-á-tor, pósci¬</l><l xml:id="m-be5c5159-5925-45fc-876b-5f45806a3828" facs="#m-d5e1667a-9d71-4b29-832f-6511cd504d90" label="lyrics-like">mus, Ut pro tú¬ a cle-ménti- a, Sis praésul et custódi-a.</l></lg>
            </div>
          </section>
        </score>
      </mdiv>
    </body>
  </music>
</mei>